  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the two Lérins islands, Sainte-Marguerite and Saint-Honorat, the Cannes tourist office lists beaches and coves "open to dogs", provided they are kept on a leash. Access is only by ferry from the port of Cannes.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The city of Cannes asks visitors to keep their dog on a leash on both islands, not to disturb the animals and to stay on the marked paths. As for the boats: Trans Côte d'Azur states that dogs are welcome on board and on Sainte-Marguerite island, on a leash, and Planaria (Saint-Honorat) accepts dogs on a leash. For the other operator on the Sainte-Marguerite line, Horizon, we found no published rule: check before booking. Smoking is banned on both islands, and waste must be taken back to the mainland.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Sainte-Marguerite is larger, ideal for a proper forest walk before the swim; Saint-Honorat, home to a monastery, is smaller and quieter.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The port of Cannes, the departure point for the ferries, is full of terraces for a break before or after the crossing.</p>
